      "source": "01 Core - applies to everyone/01-core-start-here.md",
      "id": "core/start-here",
      "route": "core/start-here/",
      "section": "core",
      "order": 1,
      "kind": "guide",
      "title": {
        "en": "Core: start here",
        "af": "Kern: begin hier"
      },
      "tags": ["orientation"],
      "sourceFixes": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "find": "the habits that stop you being scammed.\n3. Pick a name",
          "replace": "the habits that stop you being scammed.\n\n3. Pick a name",
          "reason": "The one-space-indented note after step 2 is not part of the list item, so CommonMark treats steps 3 to 7 as lazy continuation lines of that paragraph. A blank line restores the ordered list (start 3) after the note."
        },
        {
          "lang": "translations",
          "pattern": "^(2\\. [^\\n]*\\n\\n?)( ?[^\\s\\d-][^\\n]*)\\n(3\\. )",
          "replace": "$1$2\n\n$3",
          "optional": true,
          "reason": "Same quirk as the English fix above, in translated wording: the note under step 2, followed by \"3. \" on the next line, makes steps 3 to 7 part of that paragraph. A blank line restores the ordered list. Anchored to the \"2. \" line so it can only ever fix the note under step 2, never another line that happens to sit above a \"3. \". A translation that already has the blank line needs no fix."
        }
      ]
    },
